# Every lifecycle event sent through POST /trades/trigger-event, the event named as a parameter. As in the other API
# snippets the request is built in one step and sent in the next. The request is the case's own row
# (data/api/<event>.json, chosen by the case ID) with its tradeIds replaced by a stored trade. The event name, the word
# before "data" (valid, invalid, malformed, duplicate) and the optional "with '<what>'" are for the reader: they say
# what the row holds, so that the scenarios of a feature differ in their steps; the row is what is sent. The outcomes
# compare the response with the case's recording. A new event needs no snippet here: case data, recordings and the
# feature. Evidence beyond the response (notional reduced, trade closed) stays in the event's own api/<feature>.snippet.

# ── Build request ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

# On the trade of the precondition (createdTradeId).
# Example: maker has invalid data with 'an empty sub-trade list' for the 'Allocation' event
@When "^(maker|checker) has (?:valid|invalid|malformed|duplicate) data(?: with '[^']*')? for the '([^']*)' event$"
    Given build json request from current scenario with trade id from stored variable 'createdTradeId' as user '$1'

# On another stored trade, e.g. one a precondition stored under its own name.
@When "^(maker|checker) has (?:valid|invalid|malformed|duplicate) data(?: with '[^']*')? for the '([^']*)' event on the trade stored as '([^']*)'$"
    Given build json request from current scenario with trade id from stored variable '$3' as user '$1'

# The row's own tradeIds, which name no trade.
@When "^(maker|checker) has data for the '([^']*)' event on a trade that does not exist$"
    Given build json request with body from current scenario as user '$1'

# ── Make api call ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

@When "^performs the '([^']*)' event via api$"
    When post to path '/trades/trigger-event'
    And attach the response body to the report

# ── Assertions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@Then "^the '([^']*)' event is executed successfully$"
    Then the '$1' should be 'executed' successfully

@Then "^the '([^']*)' event is rejected with a validation error$"
    Then failed to 'execute' '$1'

@Then "^the '([^']*)' event is rejected with a business rule violation$"
    Then failed to 'execute' '$1'

@Then "^the '([^']*)' event is rejected with permission denied$"
    Then failed to 'execute' '$1' with status '403'
